ewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"note":"Generated by applying the repository's documented access policy to this dataset's identifiers. It is not a reviewer's account of this dataset, and a reviewed route replaces it where one exists."}]},{"order":3,"action":"Resolve the study UUID, then fetch the file manifest","detail":"filesPerStudy keys on the version UUID, not on PDC000436. Passing the PDC study id returns one row per file with every field null - a successful call that looks like a study whose files carry no metadata. Resolve the latest version through studyCatalog first. acceptDUA: true is the programmatic form of the portal's terms click; without it there are no signed download URLs.","url":"https://pdc.cancer.gov/data-dictionary/publicapi-documentation/","requires":[],"est_time":null,"cli_snippet":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport requests\nSTUDY = \"PDC000436\"\nGQL = \"https://pdc.cancer.gov/graphql\"\ncatalog = requests.post(GQL, json={\"query\": \"{ studyCatalog(acceptDUA: true) { pdc_study_id versions { study_id is_latest_version } } }\"}).json()[\"data\"][\"studyCatalog\"]\nuuid = next(v[\"study_id\"] for s in catalog if s[\"pdc_study_id\"] == STUDY\n            for v in s[\"versions\"] if v[\"is_latest_version\"] == \"yes\")\nq = '{ filesPerStudy(study_id: \"%s\" acceptDUA: true) { file_id file_name file_type data_category } }' % uuid\nfiles = requests.post(GQL, json={\"query\": q}).json()[\"data\"][\"filesPerStudy\"]\nprint(len(files), \"files\")\nPY","audience":"agent","evidence":[{"method":"derived","source_url":"https://pdc.cancer.gov/data-dictionary/publicapi-documentation/","source_label":"PDC data use guidelines","retrieved_at":"2026-09-20T15:22:08.478293Z","snippet":null,"locator":null,"confidence":"medium","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"note":"Generated by applying the repository's documented access policy to this dataset's identifiers. It is not a reviewer's account of this dataset, and a reviewed route replaces it where one exists."}]}],"analysis